This project is an independent Linux integration layer and is not affiliated
with or endorsed by Cline Bot Inc.

The upstream Cline project is distributed separately under the Apache License
2.0. This repository does not vendor the Cline source tree. The small
lib/dev-headless-loopback.ts launcher is adapted from Cline's Apache-2.0
desktop headless launcher to bind the browser/headless UI to loopback. Native
mode builds an unmodified upstream Tauri release bundle and stages its packaged
runtime locally. At install time this project may also copy an application icon
from the user's own upstream Cline checkout for local desktop-menu integration
only. The README hero is a project-created composition using nominative
`Cline` text and
the Tux artwork; it does not contain the upstream Cline source tree or official
Cline logo artwork and does not imply affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement
by Cline Bot Inc.
The Tux artwork in `assets/tux.svg` is included for Linux identification only.
It is the public-domain vector redrawing by Garrett LeSage, based on the
original artwork by Larry Ewing and refined by IFo Hancroft; it does not imply
sponsorship or endorsement by the Linux community or its organizations.
`assets/cline-linux-hero.png` is a derived raster composition for README
display.
